> Original600-point mixture

Retain centers(0,0),(6,1),(2,6),(7,7),(3,3),120 observations per center,
mt19937_64 seed12 and independent normal noise with standard deviation0.6 in x
then y. The native fixture preserves the original generator order;
standard-library normal mappings remain implementation-specific. Request16
codewords, epsilon0.01,100 Lloyd passes per size and relative tolerance1e−8 as
before.

One complete native trace contains every real stage and Lloyd update. Stage
distortion is now evaluated against that stage’s actual final codebook, making
its assignment/history/result mutually consistent. This can differ from the
legacy pre-update reported distortion while preserving the ordinary finite
split/stopping codebook path. Equal coordinate scales show the original geometry
and the actual final16 codewords; no reference class labels are fitted.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lbg_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto data = dm::algorithms::lbg_demo_mixture();
    auto t = dm::algorithms::linde_buzo_gray_trace(data, 16, .01, 100, 1e-8);
    std::print("| actual codewords | actual Lloyd updates | actual final nearest distortion | actual used " "codewords | actual tolerance stop |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (auto &s : t.stages) {
        std::vector<bool> used(s.size);
        for (auto a : s.assignment)
            used[a] = true;
        std::print("| {} | {} | {:.12f} | {} | {} |\n", s.size, s.iterations,
                   s.distortion, std::count(used.begin(), used.end(), true),
                   s.tolerance_stop);
    }
    std::print("\nOriginal points {}; actual nearest passes {}; actual point-center distances {}; actual " "coordinate squares {}; actual Lloyd updates {}; actual captured entries {}.\n",
               data.size(), t.analysis.work.assignment_passes,
               t.analysis.work.distance_evaluations,
               t.analysis.work.coordinate_squares,
               t.analysis.work.lloyd_iterations, t.captured_entries);
    std::vector<double> x, y, cx, cy;
    for (auto &p : data) {
        x.push_back(p[0]);
        y.push_back(p[1]);
    }
    for (auto &c : t.analysis.result.codebook) {
        cx.push_back(c[0]);
        cy.push_back(c[1]);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "original observations", {148, 163, 184}, 3).points(
        cx, cy, "actual codebook", {15, 23, 42}, 8).size(850, 850).margins(
        95, 35, 60, 70).x_limits(-3, 12).y_limits(-3, 12).title(
        "Original mixture and actual16-codeword LBG fit").x_label("x").y_label(
        "y").save_svg("build/lbg_original.svg");
}
```
