> Final centroids require a final nearest pass

A finite Lloyd budget can end immediately after centroid updates. The old
implementation then returned labels and distortion from the preceding codebook,
which can disagree with the returned centroids. For data0,5,6,7,8, request2 and
a single Lloyd update per size, the real two-codeword update changes centers
to2.5 and7. The point5 was assigned to the first pre-update center but is nearer
the second returned center. Final nearest distortion is2.45.

The corrected shared producer performs an actual final assignment pass at each
size; ordinary and count-only calls perform it too, and its work is counted. The
native iteration record deliberately retains its true pre-update
labels/objective, while the completed stage/result contains the final consistent
labels/objective. This consistency correction does not claim convergence: with
one pass, tolerance_stop is false. No report-side reassignment fabricates either
history.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lbg_consistency.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t =
        dm::algorithms::linde_buzo_gray_trace({{0}, {5}, {6}, {7}, {8}}, 2, .01,
                                              1, 1e-6);
    auto &i = t.iterations.back();
    auto &s = t.stages.back();
    std::print("| actual original point | actual pre-update assignment | actual final nearest assignment " "|\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t j = 0; j < t.data.size(); ++j)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", t.data[j][0], i.assignment[j],
                   s.assignment[j]);
    std::print("\nActual final centers {}, {}; actual pre-update distortion {:.12f}; actual final nearest " "distortion {:.12f}; actual tolerance stop {}.\n",
               s.final[0][0], s.final[1][0], i.before_distortion, s.distortion,
               s.tolerance_stop);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points({0, 1}, {i.before_distortion, s.distortion},
             "actual observed objectives", {37, 99, 235}, 7).x_limits(-.3, 1.3).y_limits(0, std::max(i.before_distortion, s.distortion) * 1.4).title("Actual objectives belong to different real codebooks").x_label("state0:before update; state1:final nearest pass").y_label("actual mean squared nearest distance").save_svg("build/lbg_consistency.svg");
}
```
