> Contracts and verification

Complete nonempty data is rectangular, finite and positive dimensional. Epsilon
and tolerance are finite nonnegative; Lloyd budget is positive. Empty data and
zero target retain an empty-result no-op after complete input/parameter
validation. Non-power-of-two targets round up with checked geometry. Every
produced distance, distortion, split coordinate and mean must remain
representable; ordinary finite double order is retained, with widened parallel
aggregates avoiding some centroid/distortion-sum overflow. No global optimum,
fully used/distinct centers or source-independent compression claim is made.

The actual stopping test compares consecutive pre-update distortions after
committing the new means; it is strictly previous−current<tol*(previous+1e−12),
so tolerance0 can run to the cap at an exact fixed point. Each completed stage
receives a real final nearest-codebook pass. Captured iteration labels refer to
its before codebook, not its after codebook; stage and result labels refer to
their final codebook.

Trace admission counts n*d original coordinates; each actual stage record
plus2*k*d codebook coordinates+n final assignments; each actual iteration record
plus2*k*d coordinates+n assignments+k counts. Records are admitted before their
copies, and a complete trace or exception is returned. Unknown convergence
length is not filled with invented events. Default cap is one million actual
logical records, zero disables only that optional cap, and scalar fields/row
headers/capacities/output/runtime copies/bytes are excluded. Captures own their
inputs and real states with no prefix reruns.

Native tests retain the original mixture, verify actual assignment and centroid
updates, check the stale-label correction and zero-centroid collapse, and cover
rounded targets, finite arithmetic, quotas and ownership. The ten-report batch
passed 101 native CTest cases, 34 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan cases, 103
compiled/executed public examples, 515/515 scoped file definitions plus 10 exact
LCG class definitions, and ten representative clangd hovers. Independent Python
integer/Fraction, explicit-label graph search, quadratic sequence DP and full
weighted-stump references passed 69430 records across all ten topics, including
a separately fitted held-out Iris model. Frozen ordinary compatibility passed
1000 Lex-BFS orders, 1000 library sorts, 100 LBG codebooks, 100 complete
five-round LogitBoost ensembles and 200 LLL bases; corrected LBG final
labels/objectives are intentionally excluded from historical compatibility. All
4 complete programs executed and all 4 native figures were rendered and visually
reviewed, with clipped legends corrected and rerun. HTML/Markdown
computed-result and figure-byte checks gate legacy retirement. Repeatable
receipts are retained in `build/mepml-conversion/batch-204-213/`.

> References

Y. Linde, A. Buzo and R. M. Gray(1980),
[An Algorithm for Vector Quantizer Design|https://doi.org/10.1109/TCOM.1980.1094577],
IEEE Transactions on Communications28(1),84–95. This implementation’s
multiplicative split, empty-cluster retention, finite pre-update stopping rule
and final consistency pass are stated explicitly; they do not imply globally
optimal or nested codebooks.
